    "raw": "\\*Enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 17.440 + 1.458x $10^{-3}$ T - 3.757x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 17.440x $10^{-3}$ T + 0.729x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 3.757x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 6.525</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -146.442 + 1.145x10^{-3}T + 0.144x10^{-6}T^{2} + 218.450T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -146.442 - 1.145x10^{-3}T\\ln T - 0.144x10^{-6}T^{2} + 109.225T^{-1} + 42.498x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Chase (19) who estimated enthalpy of formation at 298 K. ",
